<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Petrobras in derivatives imports talk-paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil Petrobras in derivatives imports talk-paper.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state-owned oil firm Petrobras is negotiating with the federal government the opening of the market for the import of a number of derivatives, a financial newspaper said.</p>
<p>A number of derivatives, including parafin, asphalt, petroleum coke, aliphatic solvents and naphta used in gas production, are to be imported without the prior approval of Petrobras and the National Fuel Department (DNC), Gazeta Mercantil said.</p>
</text>
